<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ethiopia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ethiopia is a country in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> with one of the longest continuous state traditions in the world. It was the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a> and its successor, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>, fought a long war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>, and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Adwa</a> in 1896 before being occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> from 1936 to 1941.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ethiopia.jpg" alt="Ethiopia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawn by User:SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ethiopia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
